{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -17 & -1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(-1-\\lambda )-1(-17) & =0 \\\\ -1-\\lambda +\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+17 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}+16 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2} & =-16 \\\\ \\lambda  & =\\pm 4\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =4\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 8\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81144" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =\\pm 4\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-1(-2) & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +6 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(6)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-8}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 2\\sqrt{2}\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm \\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-102773" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =2\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ \\left|\\begin{aligned}2-\\lambda  & 3 \\\\ -3 & 2-\\lambda \\end{aligned}\\right| & =0 \\\\ (2-\\lambda )(2-\\lambda )-3(-3) & =0 \\\\ 4-4\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+9 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-4\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-4)\\pm \\sqrt{(-4)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm \\sqrt{-36}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\pm 6\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-1\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-2\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-40429" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =2\\pm 3\\text{i}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -2 \\\\ 4 & 5-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(5-\\lambda )-4(-2) & =0 \\\\ 5-\\lambda -5\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+8 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-6\\lambda +13 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{(-6)^{2}-4(1)(13)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm \\sqrt{-16}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{6\\pm 4\\text{i}}{2} \\\\  & =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-2\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-3\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-3\\pm 3\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =3\\pm 3\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-39186" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =3\\pm 2\\text{i}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Compute the eigenvalues of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we find the matrix $\\,A-\\lambda I:$\n﻿﻿﻿\n\n$$\nA-\\lambda I=[\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nThen, we compute the characteristic equation, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A-\\lambda I) & =0 \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1-\\lambda  & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1-\\lambda \\end{aligned}| & =0 \\\\ (1-\\lambda )(1-\\lambda )-2(-1) & =0 \\\\ 1-2\\lambda +{\\lambda }^{2}+2 & =0 \\\\ {\\lambda }^{2}-2\\lambda +3 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the quadratic formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\lambda  & =\\frac{-b\\pm \\sqrt{{b}^{2}-4ac}}{2a} \\\\  & =\\frac{-(-2)\\pm \\sqrt{(-2)^{2}-4(1)(3)}}{2(1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm \\sqrt{-8}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pm 2\\text{i}\\sqrt{2}}{2} \\\\  & =1\\pm \\text{i}\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the eigenvalues are $\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}\\sqrt{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\lambda =-1\\pm 2\\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =-2\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}\\sqrt{2}"] ["math" "\\lambda =2\\pm \\text{i}"] ["math" "\\lambda =\\pm 2\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81022" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\lambda =1\\pm \\text{i}\\sqrt{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+6\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $\\frac{3}{2}({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=-4+6\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=-4-6\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =\\frac{3}{2}(-4+6\\text{i}+(-4-6\\text{i})) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}(-8) \\\\  & =-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-12"] ["math" "-18\\text{i}"] ["math" "-\\frac{16}{3}"] ["math" "12"] ["math" "18\\text{i}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-103534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-12"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${\\lambda }_{1}=6-\\text{i}$ and ${\\lambda }_{2}$ are eigenvalues of a real $2\\times 2$ matrix $A$, find $3({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since ${\\lambda }_{1}=6-\\text{i}$ is a complex eigenvalue of $A,$ the second eigenvalue of $A$ must be the complex conjugate of ${\\lambda }_{1}.$\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{2}={\\overset{―}{\\lambda }}_{1}=6+\\text{i}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3({\\lambda }_{1}+{\\lambda }_{2}) & =3(6-\\text{i}+(6+\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(12) \\\\  & =36.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb81109b1ba16b80733721d"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "3fbdccf92f21a7349d5f8d53750e5de002224031c4ed05ea7ba15dd8ed17a4ed"} {"question" "q-81036" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14040374/state.json" "file_sha256" "249efc5131146c2d107fbe719a53774a5f7c65c94cb